\tag{fdip}
\title{Dirac–Kähler operator on a cubical torus}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{The counting pairing on the cubes of a torus produces an adjoint
without inverting an integer. The square of the sum of the
coboundary and that adjoint is the Laplacian over any commutative
ring. A prime period can separate that kernel from the cohomology.}

\p{The centered kernel, the corners of its symbol, and the free
Wilson kernel remain the published comparison counts. Over an
ordered field a positive weight makes the harmonic space
isomorphic to the cohomology, both of rank #{2^d}.}

\p{The exterior algebra on the directions is the regular module
for the standard dot product. For period #{1} or #{2} every right
multiplication commutes with the counting operator. For period at
least #{3} the scalar multiplications are the ones that remain.}

